// Static site Worker "guzzionboard" (https://guzzionboard.aaron-hard11.workers.dev).
//
// This file exists so that the published file set is decided here, in git,
// instead of by wrangler's automatic project configuration at build time. With
// no config at the repository root, every Workers Builds run detected a static
// project, prompted (non-interactively: "using fallback value"), wrote a
// throwaway wrangler.jsonc, appended to .gitignore and created its own
// .assetsignore in the build container - so nothing in this repository said
// which files were on the public site.
//
// The relay is NOT this Worker and is not affected by this file: it is
// guzzionboard-validation, deployed with an explicit
// --config cloudflare/wrangler.build.toml (see scripts/deploy_worker.sh).
//
// Reverting "preview_urls": false re-enables per-version preview URLs for the
// website. It is off here on purpose: the site is served from the same account
// as the relay, and preview URLs are the default way a branch deployment gets
// published without anyone deciding to.
{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "guzzionboard",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-23",
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": false,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "."
  }
}
